Feature: Mask the last 4 digits of invoice_number in d_product_revenue_clone

  This feature implements logic to mask the last 4 digits of the invoice_number column in the purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone table using '*', in accordance with compliance policy.
  The process involves dropping the clone table if it exists, creating a full replica from the source table (d_product_revenue), and applying masking transformation on invoice_number.

  Background:
    Given Unity Catalog catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And Unity Catalog schema is "purgo_playground"
    And source table is "d_product_revenue"
    And target table is "d_product_revenue_clone"
    And target table columns are:
      | Column                         | DataType |
      | product_id                     | bigint   |
      | product_name                   | string   |
      | product_type                   | string   |
      | revenue                        | bigint   |
      | country                        | string   |
      | customer_id                    | string   |
      | purchased_date                 | date     |
      | invoice_date                   | date     |
      | invoice_number                 | bigint   |
      | is_returned                    | bigint   |
      | customer_satisfaction_score    | bigint   |
      | product_details                | string   |
      | customer_first_purchased_date  | date     |
      | customer_first_product         | string   |
      | customer_first_revenue         | double   |

  Scenario: Drop target table if it exists before replication
    Given the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" exists
    When the data masking workflow starts
    Then the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" should be dropped

  Scenario: Create clone of source table with identical schema
    Given the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" does not exist
    When the data masking workflow starts
    Then the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" should be created as an exact replica of "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue"

  Scenario Outline: Mask the last 4 digits of invoice_number during data load
    Given source table contains a row with invoice_number = <input_invoice_number>
    When data is loaded into "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"
    Then the corresponding row in "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" should have invoice_number = <expected_masked_value> as a string

    Examples:
      | input_invoice_number | expected_masked_value |
      | 1234234534           | 123423****           |
      | 9876543210           | 987654****           |
      | 1234567890123        | 1234567890****       |
      | 1234                 | ****                 |
      | 199                  | ***                  |
      | 8                    | *                    |
      | 0                    | *                    |
      | NULL                 | NULL                 |
      | -123456              | -12****              |

  Scenario: Ensure invoice_number is always a string after masking
    Given a row is inserted with invoice_number = 12345678 (bigint)
    When data is loaded and masking is applied
    Then the column invoice_number must be cast to STRING type in "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"

  Scenario: Handle NULL invoice_number gracefully
    Given a row in source table has invoice_number = NULL
    When masked data is loaded
    Then the invoice_number in target table should remain NULL

  Scenario: Handle invoice_number with fewer than 4 digits
    Given a row in source table has invoice_number = <input_invoice_number>
    When masked data is loaded
    Then the invoice_number in target table should be <expected_masked_value>

    Examples:
      | input_invoice_number | expected_masked_value |
      | 123                  | ***                  |
      | 1                    | *                    |
      | 0                    | *                    |

  Scenario: Mask negative invoice_number values
    Given a row in source table has invoice_number = <input_invoice_number>
    When masked data is loaded
    Then the invoice_number in target table should be <expected_masked_value>

    Examples:
      | input_invoice_number | expected_masked_value |
      | -5321                | -****                |
      | -75                  | -**                  |
      | -9999                | -****                |
      | -10001               | -100**               |

  Scenario: Validate error if invoice_number exceeds valid bigint range
    Given a row in source table has invoice_number = 92233720368547758070
    When data is loaded
    Then an error should be raised with message "invoice_number value exceeds valid bigint range"

  Scenario: Retain all other column values without modification
    Given a row in source table with product_id = 999, product_name = "Demo", revenue = 5000, and invoice_number = 3456789
    When data is loaded into clone table with masking flow
    Then in target table, product_id = 999, product_name = "Demo", revenue = 5000, and invoice_number = 345***, with all other columns unchanged

  Scenario: Overwrite behavior on every pipeline run
    Given "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" has prior data
    When the masking workflow is triggered
    Then existing contents in "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" should be replaced with newly masked and loaded data from source table with full overwrite

  Scenario: Restrict masking and overwrite logic only to d_product_revenue_clone
    Given tables with similar columns exist in "purgo_playground"
    When the masking workflow is triggered
    Then only "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table should be dropped, re-created, and loaded

  Scenario: Raise error if table drop fails due to permissions
    Given user does not have DROP TABLE privileges on "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"
    When the masking workflow starts
    Then an error message "Insufficient permissions to drop d_product_revenue_clone" should be raised

  Scenario: Masking logic does not impact source table data
    Given data in "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue"
    When the masking workflow completes
    Then original values in "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue" table, including invoice_number, remain unchanged

  Scenario: Ensure masked values conform to the following validation rules
    Given the pipeline has loaded data into clone table
    Then each value in invoice_number must match:
      | Rule                                                   |
      | If invoice_number is NULL, output is NULL              |
      | If abs(invoice_number) >= 4 digits, last 4 replaced by '*' |
      | If abs(invoice_number) < 4 digits, all digits replaced by '*' per digit |
      | Output is always string type, retains sign if negative |
